  "steps": [
    "In a large bowl, mix the turkey mince, egg, grated red onion, minced garlic, parsley, oregano, cumin, salt and black pepper until just combined. Form into 16 small meatballs.",
    "Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil in a large deep pan over medium heat. Brown the meatballs in batches for 5 to 6 minutes, turning so they colour on several sides. Transfer them to a plate; they do not need to be cooked through.",
    "Add the remaining olive oil to the same pan. Cook the chopped onion for 5 minutes until soft and lightly golden, then add the sliced garlic for 30 seconds.",
    "Stir in the canned tomatoes, tomato paste, water and thyme. Bring to a simmer, scraping up any browned bits from the pan.",
    "Return the meatballs to the sauce, cover partially, and simmer gently for 12 to 15 minutes until the meatballs are cooked through and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Stir in the lemon juice and sprinkle over the fresh parsley. Serve hot, with rice, potatoes or crusty bread if desired."
